                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1b04ef84-a549-3b62-bccf-315047bc4ba8",
                        "entry_id": "19d74139-7c49-304b-a979-285d2cf26869",
                        "glosses": [
                            "cecha tego, co jest nieprzekupne; cecha tych, którzy są nieprzekupni"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b4629248-9922-4885-8c8b-df960ff2b1ad",
                                "sense_id": "1b04ef84-a549-3b62-bccf-315047bc4ba8",
                                "text": "Nadaje się na psa stróżującego dzięki nieprzekupności i wrodzonej niechęci do obcych"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "09b36295-92fc-453e-a192-35f8614a59f8",
                        "source_entry_id": "19d74139-7c49-304b-a979-285d2cf26869",
                        "source_sense_id": "1b04ef84-a549-3b62-bccf-315047bc4ba8",
                        "target_lang_word": "incorruptibility",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "incorruptibility",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "78527d03-75a2-3b7c-b030-0d07da160869",
                                        "entry_id": "41234499-2c7e-3118-bafa-4f6d5282880d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of being incorruptible; honesty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "397a7a61-c834-4986-9b5d-9a153b236da3",
                                                "sense_id": "78527d03-75a2-3b7c-b030-0d07da160869",
                                                "text": "In short—which is the strongest proof that can be given of the excellence of her heart, and the incorruptibility of her honour, she, at eighteen, was as spotless a character at Little Hockley, as the most innocent inhabitant of her age and sex could be at Castlewick."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a668a4c6-f1f6-450a-9d2f-8fcd77b700c7",
                                                "sense_id": "78527d03-75a2-3b7c-b030-0d07da160869",
                                                "text": "Nowadays, with our modern mania for morality, every one has to pose as a paragon of purity, incorruptibility, and all the other seven deadly virtues—and what is the result? You all go over like ninepins—one after the other."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8633419-ef31-4ee1-93b0-7bcc8a55744b",
                                                "sense_id": "78527d03-75a2-3b7c-b030-0d07da160869",
                                                "text": "In South Africa men are proud of their Judges, because they believe they are incorruptible. Even the black men have faith in them, though they do not always have faith in the Law. In a land of fear this incorruptibility is like a lamp set upon a stand, giving light to all that are in the house."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65de2a68-e3f5-317d-a2ab-4c3d8e7d00fd",
                                        "entry_id": "41234499-2c7e-3118-bafa-4f6d5282880d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The condition of never decaying or decomposing (especially, as ascribed to the bodies of holy people in Roman Catholic and Eastern Orthodox Christianity)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7af09966-0915-4b28-a106-b3178ac626a2",
                                                "sense_id": "65de2a68-e3f5-317d-a2ab-4c3d8e7d00fd",
                                                "text": "1618, Anonymous translator, A Manuall of Devout Meditations and Exercises by Tomás de Villacastín, Book 3, Meditation 12, Point 1, p. 510, facsimile reprint in D. M. Rogers (editor), English Recusant Literature, 1558-1640, Volume 326, Menston: The Scolar Press, 1976,\nGather hence great joy at the Resurrection of the B. Virgin, and the incorruptibility of her body, the rare and speciall priviledge graunted unto her by her most holy Son, who fullfilled the desires of her soule."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d154c044-fb41-4d32-952a-1804e7b6710f",
                                                "sense_id": "65de2a68-e3f5-317d-a2ab-4c3d8e7d00fd",
                                                "text": "The Being of a God, and Incorruptibility of the Soul, those great Articles of Religion, are they not proved with the clearest and most immediate Evidence?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57cc2a7e-a7c2-4a06-bee7-d28c7d59cfde",
                                                "sense_id": "65de2a68-e3f5-317d-a2ab-4c3d8e7d00fd",
                                                "text": "The PEACOCK, in ancient times, was possessed of a mystic character. The fabled incorruptibility of its flesh led to its typifying the Resurrection; and from this incorruptibility, doubtless, originated the first idea of swearing “by the Peacock,” an oath that was to be inviolably kept."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e8bd6034-d348-4c1f-8901-371aefc833a4",
                        "source_entry_id": "19d74139-7c49-304b-a979-285d2cf26869",
                        "source_sense_id": "1b04ef84-a549-3b62-bccf-315047bc4ba8",
                        "target_lang_word": "incorruptibilité",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "incorruptibilité",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e28440f-9da6-3e5c-9a02-93b3ff895f53",
                                        "entry_id": "d858b21f-84ba-3456-86a8-ec674ef38554",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qualité de ce qui est incorruptible, de ce qui ne se corrompt pas."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73f1e8bc-18eb-43cd-a88d-ff1190758a47",
                                                "sense_id": "7e28440f-9da6-3e5c-9a02-93b3ff895f53",
                                                "text": "Il faut que ce corps corruptible soit revêtu d'incorruptibilité, et que ce corps mortel soit revêtu de l'immortalité."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93393658-e518-41f6-a9ba-c717bb2d791e",
                                                "sense_id": "7e28440f-9da6-3e5c-9a02-93b3ff895f53",
                                                "text": "Ils ont cessé de percevoir à la fois la menace du vide et le poids de leur chair périssable. Quelque chose de l’ardeur et de l’incorruptibilité des hauteurs est passé dans leur sang."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e508cb21-29c6-3897-98ab-aecef0b3b5ce",
                                        "entry_id": "d858b21f-84ba-3456-86a8-ec674ef38554",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Phénomène par lequel le corps de certains saints reste intact après leur mort."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c9c13af-5272-446f-8677-70e535d4e28c",
                                                "sense_id": "e508cb21-29c6-3897-98ab-aecef0b3b5ce",
                                                "text": "Enfin, trente-quatre ans après sa mort, l'incorruptibilité de son corps (constatée par l'ouverture de son cercueil en 2002 lors de sa canonisation par Jean-Paul II), qu'on a pu également constater chez Bernadette Soubirous, est un autre phénomène contraire aux lois biologiques, portant de nombreux fidèles catholiques à croire en une force supérieure invisible."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "772aabd1-23ee-3e77-ad1f-a62b7bfbc0a4",
                                        "entry_id": "d858b21f-84ba-3456-86a8-ec674ef38554",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qualité de ce qui ne peut être altéré, modifié."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7662b210-c289-4a45-9f59-998f0f3a737d",
                                                "sense_id": "772aabd1-23ee-3e77-ad1f-a62b7bfbc0a4",
                                                "text": "Cet impôt [la dîme royale] surpasse les autres infiniment par son abondance, par sa simplicité, par la justesse de sa proportion, et par son incorruptibilité."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6fd2182d-8860-475a-a611-26170df3eab1",
                                                "sense_id": "772aabd1-23ee-3e77-ad1f-a62b7bfbc0a4",
                                                "text": "L'incorruptibilité convient mieux à la loi naturelle qu'à aucune autre."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3cb4166-f5f2-4367-8066-288e0c22c632",
                                                "sense_id": "772aabd1-23ee-3e77-ad1f-a62b7bfbc0a4",
                                                "text": "— Je vous réponds de votre incorruptibilité [que la province ne vous gâtera pas] tant que vous serez ensemble [Bussy et sa fille]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b7a428b-8da4-305d-bc6a-32b2b3e75f7a",
                                        "entry_id": "d858b21f-84ba-3456-86a8-ec674ef38554",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Intégrité d'une personne incapable de se laisser corrompre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82707c4e-53a8-4186-9e8e-a3715454a9a4",
                                                "sense_id": "6b7a428b-8da4-305d-bc6a-32b2b3e75f7a",
                                                "text": "J'accorderai à Emile Combes le caractère, la volonté, je m'inclinerai devant son incorruptibilité."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0056bce-1267-4717-971b-e3423dc26158",
                                                "sense_id": "6b7a428b-8da4-305d-bc6a-32b2b3e75f7a",
                                                "text": "Elle l’avait appelé Fidélio, et comme l’employé de mairie trouvait le nom difficile, elle lui donna deux francs qu’il accepta. Ce fut ma première désillusion à l’endroit de l’incorruptibilité des fonctionnaires."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "900a1a68-3647-4bb9-a3d2-7744028fd93d",
                                                "sense_id": "6b7a428b-8da4-305d-bc6a-32b2b3e75f7a",
                                                "text": "De temps à autre, une voix s’élevait pour demander son renvoi, qui semblait d’autant plus justifié qu’il n’avait ni une réputation d’incorruptibilité ni l’alibi de la compétence."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
